@@ -351,6 +351,9 @@ The `data/secondmates.md` line contract is owned by the [`secondmate-provisionin
 `no-mistakes` tasks run the full validation pipeline, `direct-PR` tasks open PRs without that pipeline, and `local-only` tasks stay local until firstmate performs an approved fast-forward merge.
 Opt-in `agent-kit` tasks are judged by agent-kit's bound lifecycle and delivered by no-mistakes with its review, document, and rebase steps skipped.
 `bin/fm-agent-kit-lib.sh` owns that binding: it parses `config/agent-kit.env` without sourcing it, runs `ak firstmate bind` when the brief or promotion is written, and merges agent-kit's worker hooks into a claude launch's per-task settings file; any failure refuses the brief, promotion, or spawn.
+It also reads the binding's `delivery.action`: `publish` keeps the transport contract, while `dry-run` renders a Definition of done that publishes nothing.
+It runs Firstmate's own audit of an agent-kit `done:` through `ak firstmate status <binding> --verify`, and a refused or unrunnable audit becomes a `needs-decision` rather than a done.
+An optional `AK_FIRSTMATE_WORKER_BUDGET_USD` bounds the claude worker with `--max-budget-usd`.
 Each task's mode and `yolo` merge posture are firstmate's decision at intake.
 The mode is passed explicitly to `bin/fm-brief.sh`, and both values are passed explicitly to `bin/fm-spawn.sh` and `bin/fm-promote.sh`; each command refuses to guess the values it consumes.
 A ship brief records its mode as a fixed machine-readable line and the spawn refuses to launch on a different one, so the worker's instructions and the recorded task delivery cannot diverge.
